" Fjord " director Cristian Mungiu insists that audiences should make up their own minds about his polarizing Palme d'Or winner, which divided critics as much as it united the jury at this year's Cannes Film Festival.

The film, which pits a conservative Christian couple against a progressive social system, has become something of a Rorschach test for audiences since it premiered on the Croisette, where Variety &#x2019;s chief film critic Guy Lodge praised it as a &#x201C;superb new drama of systemic order and individual disarray." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Disney Expected to Lay Off Thousands of Staffers in Biggest Round of Cuts This Year Disney+ and Hulu App Merger Slated to Be Complete in December

&#x201C;The film is not divisive. The society is divided. And the film is about this,&#x201D; Mungiu said Monday at the Marrakech Film Festival . &#x201C;It&#x2019;s just normal that when people watch the film, they will be as divided as they are in their society, and this is what the film is about. The film is about this incapacity of us sharing the same society with people who do not share the same views as us.&#x201D;

"Fjord" follows Mihai (Sebastian Stan) and Lisvet (Renate Reinsve), two Evangelical Christians who leave Mihai&#x2019;s homeland in Romania and, along with their five children, move to Lisbet&#x2019;s native Norway. There, they establish themselves in a small village, where they hope to give their children a quieter, gentler way of life. But when their eldest daughter turns up to gym class with bruises on her body, the family becomes mired in a child abuse case that pits the couple against a Norwegian social system determined to wrest custody of the children away from them.

Even while winning the Palme in Cannes , &#x201C;Fjord&#x201D; was among the more hotly debated titles in the competition lineup, with critics divided on whether Mungiu&#x2019;s complex moral drama sided more with the conservative values of its protagonists or the progressive mores of Norwegian society. In his analysis of the polarizing discourse around the film, Variety &#x2019;s Owen Gleiberman noted that it &#x201C;cuts to the spiritual-ideological heart of so much of what&#x2019;s happening today.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Appearing in conversation with Sydney Film Festival director Nashen Moodley, Mungiu &#x2014; who introduced "Fjord" to a capacity audience at the Marrakech festival on Sunday night &#x2014; was asked about how his film has been claimed by left- and right-wing audiences alike, and whether those who have positioned it as a &#x201C;MAGA film&#x201D; have misread his intent. Mungiu replied, &#x201C;I think that some people misread reality.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I think that it is important to use cinema also to encourage people to think &#x2014; not to tell them what to think,&#x201D; he continued. &#x201C;We stopped being used to watching such films in which the conclusion is not already in the film, in which we are not told already we are on the good side of things, and the director tells us precisely what is good, what is wrong. That&#x2019;s a kind of filmmaking. You can make films like this if you want.

